# Append-mostly files that nearly every pull request edits at the same place
# (the end of a table, the top of [Unreleased]). A local merge or rebase keeps
# both sides' lines instead of stopping on a conflict. GitHub's own merge does
# not use this driver; it helps the `git rebase origin/dev` that resolves the
# conflict GitHub reports.
#
# Safe only where a duplicated line is caught or harmless:
# - the decision log: a row edited on both sides comes out twice, and
#   scripts/docs/check-decision-ids.sh (in `Repo: checks`) fails on the
#   duplicate ID;
# - the changelog: entries are appended; a bullet edited on both sides comes
#   out twice, which review sees in the diff.
# Not for generated files (docs/house/*, SDK facades, lockfiles): regenerate
# those after a rebase instead.
docs/design/13-decision-log.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
